  "created": "2026-11-20T10:58:06.403Z",
  "description": "ExpertPdf PDF Security Library protects PDF documents with passwords and permissions, removes the protection of documents you have the password of, and signs documents with digital certificates.\n\nThis package contains the library for .NET Framework 2.0 to 4.8.1, .NET Core 2.0+ and .NET 5 to .NET 11 (through .NET Standard 2.0).\n\nFeatures\n- User and owner passwords; print, copy, edit, form fill and assemble permissions\n- RC4 and AES encryption with 40, 128 or 256 bit keys\n- Remove the security of protected documents\n- Digital signatures with PKCS#12 certificates, with time stamps from a time stamp authority\n- From and to files, streams or byte arrays; thread safe",
  "iconFile": "images\\icon.jpg",
  "id": "ExpertPdf.PdfSecurity",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-20T11:10:00.67Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ZmT33TzEsM6yz/8NX8DXH/09LNjxOm9CODNdjxeQ+Vyl1/r/XJ/LGouCJJzrITVH9woAem6yOOyCRXYmp07NUA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 5755216,
  "projectUrl": "https://www.html-to-pdf.net/",
  "published": "2026-11-20T10:58:06.403Z",
  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 10.0: Sign from a stream to a stream and from bytes to bytes. SourcePdfPassword: process password protected sources. ValidateSignatures: integrity, certificate chain, time stamp and revocation of every signature. GetSecurityInfo: encryption, permissions and signatures of a document without changing it. Certification signatures (CertificationLevel) and AddSignatureField; signing with AES-256 encrypted PFX files. Version 10 is part of the ExpertPdf 22.0 release: it requires a version 10 license key.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "Encrypt, decrypt and digitally sign PDF documents in any .NET application.",
  "title": "ExpertPdf PDF Security Library for .NET",
  "verbatimVersion": "10.0.0",
